Visual Workflow Overview

## Slide 2

Concept Overview

Definition of Workflow
A sequence of processes that create or add value
Example Workflow
When a Job Ends, set a Job on hold, schedule a QC check, and notify the QC team.
If the QC check is late, re-notify the QC team.
When the Task is completed, update the Job Status and continue the process.

## Slide 3

Implied Workflow

Production Monitoring
Detect Job completion and similar triggers.
Scripting and CPI
Business rule logic, decision making, timing, state storage and execution.
Task Management
Define required tasks, inputs and triggers.
Electronic Forms
Form user interfaces and data structures.
Messaging and Notification
Define messages, user groups, and send notifications.

## Slide 4

Visual Workflow

## Slide 5

Workflow Service

Decision Control and Orchestration Engine
Executes Processes over long periods of time
Records Process Logs and execution history
Designed to be stateless to withstand restarts and outages without disrupting business logic
Supports versioning and parallel execution of Processes

Supports Multiple and/or Distributed Instances

## Slide 6

Process Definitions

Represent configurable workflows to be executed
A Process represents an execution of a workflow with associated set of logs and history records
Processes consist of a set of Process Steps that determine the logical flow and sequences
Each Process can be provided a set of parameters for use in the workflow logic
A DbProcessSinkStart record determines when a Process is started.

Configuration

Loaded and executed by the Workflow Service
Processes contain reference to execution information such as ProcessSteps, ProcessLogs, ProcessParameters, etc…
Multiple executions of a Process Definition can be active at once, and each could be a different version

Execution

## Slide 7

Process Definitions: Examples

Concept: 
Route product information to multiple users for input and approval
Escape Logic: 
None
Parameters:
Product ID

Concept: 
Check for inventory allocated to a job, schedule and verify inventory movement
Escape Logic: 
Job is rescheduled
Parameters:
Job ID

Concept: 
Send notifications to increasingly larger groups after set intervals
Escape Logic: 
Triggering workflow kills the process
Parameters:
Notification Target IDs
Interval Durations

Product Approval

Inventory Processing

Notification Escalations

