## Slide 19

Starting Processes

A Process can be started…

… through standard pages for testing

… through standard API for execution

## Slide 20

Process Visualization

Workflows Related to Manufacturing Entities
Real-Time view of a Specific Process Execution
Steps that have already been Executed
Steps that are currently Executing
Steps that have not yet been Executed

## Slide 21

Process Steps

When a Process is started, a Process Step record is created for each Process Step Definition of the parent Process Definition
Each Process Step contains an Execution State to display the step’s current activity, including the following states
Complete Error/Success/Timeout
Executing Waiting/InScript
None
These states are used to in when visualizing the steps of a process

## Slide 22

Process Step History

Process Steps can execute multiple times during a single Process execution
Each time a Process Step executes, a Process Step History will be created
Process Step History records contain the timestamps and state data for a single execution of a Process Step

## Slide 23

Ending Processes

A Process can be ended…

… through standard pages

… through standard API

… naturally by reaching an end

context.Api.Workflow
	.KillProcess(processID)
	.ThrowIfFailed();

